Limine 9.6.7, as the fluxOS CD and installed disks boot it
==========================================================

These files are Limine's (https://limine-bootloader.org), built by Limine's
own release process and checked in so that the CD can be made without
Limine's build or a download (by mkiso, on Linux or on fluxOS itself). They
are the binary release v9.6.7, commit ee5d29cd0a8034612dcd1df3f00052480db785c5
of the v9.x-binary branch of https://github.com/limine-bootloader/limine,
unchanged; SHA256SUMS lists every file's hash, and LICENSE is Limine's
(BSD 2-clause).

  limine-bios.sys      Limine itself for a BIOS: read by its first stages
                       from /boot/limine on the CD, or on the partition the
                       kernel is on (FAT32, or the CD's ISO 9660: Limine
                       reads no other filesystems).
  limine-bios-cd.bin   the CD's El Torito boot image (no emulation), which
                       mkiso -b gives a boot information table.
  limine-uefi-cd.bin   a FAT image holding Limine for UEFI firmware: the
                       CD's El Torito entry for the EFI platform, and the
                       EFI partition of the image written to a USB stick
                       (mkiso -e, -P).
  BOOTX64.EFI          Limine for 64-bit UEFI firmware, which fluxinstall
                       copies to /EFI/BOOT on an installed disk's FAT32
                       partition.

Limine's first stages for a hard disk (its boot sector and what follows it)
are not files here: they are built into Limine's own installer,
third_party/limine/limine.c with limine-bios-hdd.h, from the same release.
"limine bios-install DISK" writes them into the MBR and the sectors before
the first partition, keeping the partition table. The build makes the
installer for the machine it runs on (build/host/limine, which makes
fluxOS.iso start from a USB stick too) and for fluxOS (/bin/limine, which
fluxinstall runs on the disk it installs to).

The kernel speaks the Limine boot protocol (kernel/core/limine.h,
bootinfo.c): Limine loads it as a 64-bit ELF image, maps it and starts it
in long mode. The menus are limine/install.conf (the CD's) and
limine/limine.conf (an installed disk's).

To move to another Limine release, replace these four files and the two in
third_party/limine from its binary branch, and make SHA256SUMS again:

  git clone --depth 1 --branch v9.x-binary https://github.com/limine-bootloader/limine
